From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove@yandex.ru>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:24:53 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 133/202] Meridian: the Windows installer has a window
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Chromium's installer shows nothing: Google's is run by another program
that has the window. A person who opened Meridian's saw no sign that it
had started, for the minute it takes, and none that it had failed.

mini_installer now shows a small window of its own while it works:
Meridian's icon, "Installing Meridian…" (or "Updating Meridian…" when the
in-app updater runs it) and a moving bar, then "Opening Meridian…". When
the installer fails, a message says so, with the error number and where the
log is; the updater, which tries again by itself, gets no message.

The window is on a thread of its own in meridian_progress.cc: plain Win32
and no C runtime, like the rest of mini_installer. Chromium's files get two
calls in the entry point, the sources and two system libraries in
BUILD.gn, and the installer's icon, which is now Meridian's.

Chromium's installer opens the browser after a first install only. Run by
a person over a copy they had, it now opens Meridian too.

--meridian-no-ui: no window. --meridian-ui-demo: the window for a few
seconds and nothing installed (--meridian-ui-demo-failure: the message
too), for looking at it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
